rewritten-to-match
Same LRU cache and the same operation sequence (the reference's key text "item_N", two lookups on a hit and on a miss, eviction of the tail when full, the same linked-list moves). The reference's HashMap<String, usize> is lib/strmap.mito (chained hash map over plain arrays, keys up to 64 bytes); the node vector with its free list is arrays indexed by the map's entry number, so removing the oldest removes the map entry by number instead of by key (one hash less than the reference's remove). Value texts ("updated_<run>" / "new_<run>") are built into a byte array slot on every put, as the reference's format! allocates one; the reference's run id is the benchmark's iteration number, here a counter that restarts at the timed run (the text does not enter the checksum). Stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback.
